      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum recommended metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (some references say 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose. Tell me the intended dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me and I'll add a note documenting that you've confirmed it. I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
